"""Triton implementation of aten::index_reduce.out.

Logical view: self/out are (L, C, T) with d = dim, source is (L, K, T) and
index is a 1-D vector of length K whose values index the C axis.

    out[l, i, t] = combine(self[l, i, t] (if include_self),
                           {source[l, j, t] : index[j] == i})

reduce semantics (matching aten):
  prod : out = self * prod(src)                 (identity 1)
  mean : out = (self + sum(src)) / (1 + n_i)     (identity 0)
  amax : out = max(self, max(src))               (identity -inf)
  amin : out = min(self, min(src))               (identity +inf)
Untouched columns (n_i == 0):
  include_self=True  -> out == self (all reduces)
  include_self=False -> out == self as well (reference semantics), handled by
                        the single-writer scan path.
"""

